 "traditions": [],
 "notes": "Kept both old kinds (k142 DJ turntable, k141 DJ controller); added DJ media player, DJ mixer, DJ cartridge. Controller list trimmed from 19 to 12 models plus archetype versions: dropped duplicate 'Traktor Z1 MK2', Reloop Buddy and Ready, DDJ-FLX2 (entry-level duplicates); DDJ-REV7, DDJ-FLX10, XDJ-RX3 moved into archetypes. Turntable ranges SL1200/SL1500/SL50 dropped as redundant with models. Standalone all-in-ones are a type and archetypes (XDJ-RX, Prime 4). Left out: Allen & Heath Xone:62/96/DB4 and year of Xone:92 (allen-heath.com returned 403), Rane TTM 56/57 and Sixty-Two/Seventy (no retrieved page), Shure Whitelabel and M44-7 launch year, Ortofon Nightclub/Scratch lines, DJM-600/900/V10/S rotary series, XDJ-RX2, PMC-05 per-model years (Vestax page gives none), Stanton ST-150 (snippet only). Clones are a maker-free 'OEM direct-drive DJ deck' archetype sourced to a Bonedo review naming Hanpin; only the RP-5000 MK4 is linked to it as a version, other clones stay in m. djworx.com returned 503."
}